---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What are "spikes" in this project?',
    answer: "Instead of measuring every tiny moment nonstop, a spiking neural network reacts to brief pulses (\"spikes\") when meaningful voltage changes happen—inspired by how real neurons communicate.",
  },
  {
    question: "Are you testing on real people or live patients?",
    answer: "No—the project uses established, open-access ECG heartbeat datasets (like MIT-BIH) rather than live patient testing, focusing on how efficiently a compact model can classify beat patterns on hardware.",
  },
  {
    question: "Why use an FPGA chip instead of a regular computer or phone?",
    answer: "An FPGA is a flexible chip whose internal logic can be tailored for low-power, real-time tasks—helping explore how energy-smart event-driven models can fit onto tight hardware limits.",
  },
  {
    question: "What do the heartbeat categories (N, S, V, F, Q) mean in plain English?",
    answer: "They are standard clinical beat groupings (such as normal rhythms versus different kinds of irregular or unclassifiable beats) used to test whether a lightweight model can tell heartbeat shapes apart reliably.",
  },
];
---

<section class="mt-7" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
  <p class="leading-relaxed text-white/80">A few quick answers to common questions about the capstone.</p>
  <dl class="mt-5 divide-y divide-white/10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] px-5">
    {faqs.map((faq) => (
      <div class="py-4">
        <dt class="font-semibold text-white">{faq.question}</dt>
        <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/70">{faq.answer}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>
</section>
